# Code owners: who must review changes to which paths.
# The last matching line wins. Owners need write access to the repository.
#
# These teams belong to the GitHub organization `liquidlyf`, so this file
# takes effect once the repository lives at github.com/liquidlyf/LiquidLyf.

# Everything, by default
*                               @liquidlyf/maintainers

# Security-sensitive: the data rules, the backend and CI/CD
/firebase/                      @liquidlyf/maintainers
/backend/                       @liquidlyf/maintainers
/.github/                       @liquidlyf/maintainers

# Medical logic: eligibility, compatibility, status changes
**/core/domain/                 @liquidlyf/maintainers

# Licence and trademark files
/LICENSE                        @liquidlyf/maintainers
/LICENSING.md                   @liquidlyf/maintainers
/TRADEMARKS.md                  @liquidlyf/maintainers

# Add these teams when they have members, then uncomment:
# /firebase/                    @liquidlyf/backend @liquidlyf/maintainers
# /backend/                     @liquidlyf/backend @liquidlyf/maintainers
# **/core/domain/               @liquidlyf/medical-review @liquidlyf/maintainers
# **/values-bn/                 @liquidlyf/translators-bn
